{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.HabiroMagnitudeA3","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MassTheory.HabiroMagnitudeA3","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.QIntegerCanonical"],"declarations":21,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.HabiroMagnitudeA3.no_bracketing_qInt_eq_rStar","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.HabiroMagnitudeA3.no_bracketing_qInt_eq_rStar","kind":"theorem","line":239,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/HabiroMagnitudeA3.lean#L239-L245","doc":"Consequently no `[k]_q` for `k ∈ {1, 2}` — the two quantum integers bracketing `r*` — can\nequal it; the α_EM-shape's leading factor cannot supply `r*` at any `q > 1` with\n`q + q⁻¹ ≥ 2` (0-fit). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.HabiroMagnitudeA3.rStar_strictly_between_q1_q2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.HabiroMagnitudeA3.rStar_strictly_between_q1_q2","kind":"theorem","line":227,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/HabiroMagnitudeA3.lean#L227-L237","doc":"**MAIN (scope-(a) bracketing of the finite sub-case).** The required `r*` lies STRICTLY\nbetween the quantum integers `[1]_q = 1` and `[2]_q = q + q⁻¹` for any `q` with\n`q + q⁻¹ ≥ 2` — in particular for the substrate `q₀ > 1`, where `q₀ + q₀⁻¹ ≈ 2.01 ≥ 2`. Since\n`r* ∈ (3/2, 2)` and the α_EM-shape finite Habiro element evaluates (to leading order) to a\nquantum integer `[k]_q`, no integer `k` lands on `r*`: `[1]_q = 1 < 3/2 < r* < 2 ≤ [2]_q`. A\nvalue hitting `r*` requires a NON-forced (fit) coefficient. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.HabiroMagnitudeA3.qInt_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.HabiroMagnitudeA3.qInt_two","kind":"theorem","line":218,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/HabiroMagnitudeA3.lean#L218-L225","doc":"`[2]_q = q + q⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.HabiroMagnitudeA3.qInt_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.HabiroMagnitudeA3.qInt_one","kind":"theorem","line":212,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/HabiroMagnitudeA3.lean#L212-L216","doc":"`[1]_q = 1` exactly. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.HabiroMagnitudeA3.denom_ne","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.HabiroMagnitudeA3.denom_ne","kind":"theorem","line":205,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/HabiroMagnitudeA3.lean#L205-L210","doc":"`q − q⁻¹ ≠ 0` for `q > 1` (since `q⁻¹ < 1 < q`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.HabiroMagnitudeA3.qInt_eq_canonical","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.HabiroMagnitudeA3.qInt_eq_canonical","kind":"theorem","line":198,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/HabiroMagnitudeA3.lean#L198-L203","doc":"**Bridge to the canonical balanced bracket.** The alias was refused — a proof\nbelow needs this literal body, with the inverse written `(q^n)⁻¹` rather than\n`q⁻¹^n` — so the consolidation is this equation rather than a substitution. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.HabiroMagnitudeA3.qInt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.HabiroMagnitudeA3.qInt","kind":"def","line":193,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/HabiroMagnitudeA3.lean#L193-L196","doc":"The balanced quantum integer `[n]_q = (q^n − q^{-n})/(q − q^{-1})`, written with real\ninverse powers `(q^n)⁻¹ = q^{-n}`. The α_EM-shape finite Habiro element `[k]_q·(1 − h²X)` has\nthis as its dominant factor (the correction `(1−h²X)` is `≈ 1` for the categorical `X`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.HabiroMagnitudeA3.rStar_lt_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.HabiroMagnitudeA3.rStar_lt_two","kind":"theorem","line":190,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/HabiroMagnitudeA3.lean#L190-L191","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.HabiroMagnitudeA3.rStar_gt_three_halves","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.HabiroMagnitudeA3.rStar_gt_three_halves","kind":"theorem","line":187,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/HabiroMagnitudeA3.lean#L187-L188","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.HabiroMagnitudeA3.rStar","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.HabiroMagnitudeA3.rStar","kind":"def","line":184,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/HabiroMagnitudeA3.lean#L184-L185","doc":"The required A=3 magnitude factor `r* = μ₃ / c₃ ≈ 1.585`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.HabiroMagnitudeA3.mu3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.HabiroMagnitudeA3.mu3","kind":"def","line":181,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/HabiroMagnitudeA3.lean#L181-L182","doc":"Target additive-residual moment `μ₃ = +0.4708 MeV` (#4320). Mirrors `VassilievMagnitudeA3.mu3`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.HabiroMagnitudeA3.c3bare","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.HabiroMagnitudeA3.c3bare","kind":"def","line":178,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/HabiroMagnitudeA3.lean#L178-L179","doc":"Hecke-level near-miss `c₃ = +0.297 MeV` (#4364). Mirrors `VassilievMagnitudeA3.c3bare`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.HabiroMagnitudeA3.habiro_terms_not_tendsto_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.HabiroMagnitudeA3.habiro_terms_not_tendsto_zero","kind":"theorem","line":153,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/HabiroMagnitudeA3.lean#L153-L174","doc":"**Term test / non-summability.** A genuine (infinite) integer-coefficient Habiro element\n`F(q) = Σ a_n (q;q)_n` with `|a_n| ≥ 1` for all `n` has terms whose magnitude is unbounded at\n`q > 1` (each `|a_n · (q;q)_n| ≥ |(q;q)_n|`), so the terms do NOT tend to `0` and the series\ndiverges. Therefore no well-defined archimedean value exists at the substrate `q₀ > 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.HabiroMagnitudeA3.pochAbs_unbounded","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.HabiroMagnitudeA3.pochAbs_unbounded","kind":"theorem","line":134,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/HabiroMagnitudeA3.lean#L134-L149","doc":"**OBSTRUCTION (the core structural fact).** For real `q > 1` the Habiro cyclotomic basis\nmagnitude `|(q;q)_n|` is UNBOUNDED: it exceeds any bound `B` at some index. Hence the\ncyclotomic-completion series `Σ a_n (q;q)_n` cannot converge at `q > 1` with non-decaying\ncoefficients — the substrate anchor `q₀ > 1` lies outside the Habiro ring's evaluation locus. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.HabiroMagnitudeA3.pochAbs_ge_geometric","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.HabiroMagnitudeA3.pochAbs_ge_geometric","kind":"theorem","line":116,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/HabiroMagnitudeA3.lean#L116-L132","doc":"Geometric doubling: once every factor is `≥ 2` (from index `N`), the basis magnitude at\n`N + m` is at least `2^m` times its value at `N`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.HabiroMagnitudeA3.exists_factor_ge_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.HabiroMagnitudeA3.exists_factor_ge_two","kind":"theorem","line":101,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/HabiroMagnitudeA3.lean#L101-L114","doc":"For `q > 1` the powers `q^n → ∞`, so eventually `q^n ≥ 3`; concretely there is an index\n`N` beyond which every subsequent cyclotomic factor exceeds `2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.HabiroMagnitudeA3.pochAbs_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.HabiroMagnitudeA3.pochAbs_pos","kind":"theorem","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/HabiroMagnitudeA3.lean#L92-L97","doc":"The basis magnitude is strictly positive for `q > 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.HabiroMagnitudeA3.factor_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.HabiroMagnitudeA3.factor_pos","kind":"theorem","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/HabiroMagnitudeA3.lean#L87-L90","doc":"Each factor `q^(n+1) − 1` is strictly positive for `q > 1` (since `q^(n+1) ≥ q > 1`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.HabiroMagnitudeA3.pochAbs_succ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.HabiroMagnitudeA3.pochAbs_succ","kind":"theorem","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/HabiroMagnitudeA3.lean#L84-L85","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.HabiroMagnitudeA3.pochAbs_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.HabiroMagnitudeA3.pochAbs_zero","kind":"theorem","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/HabiroMagnitudeA3.lean#L82-L82","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.HabiroMagnitudeA3.pochAbs","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.HabiroMagnitudeA3.pochAbs","kind":"def","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/HabiroMagnitudeA3.lean#L76-L80","doc":"Magnitude of the cyclotomic Pochhammer `(q;q)_n = ∏_{k=1}^n (1 − q^k)` for real `q > 1`,\nwhere each factor's magnitude is `q^k − 1`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}